From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0027] sensorhub/ssp: kernel-coordinated BCM47752 firmware download (rebased on 0023)

Contains ONLY the downloader, rebased on 0023.  Does NOT re-declare any
native-peer symbol 0023 already owns.  Supersedes original 0026 (raw-SSI ROM
sync) and bring-up half of 0025 (regulator_force_disable), folded in rather
than duplicated.

Corrections vs. original 0027 (compile-verified on commit f7194c1d15ed):
  - bbd_do_transfer deadlock               -> fixed in 0023.
  - Premature parser success               -> dl_next_record TRUNCATED/MALFORMED
      status hard-fails; never reaches WHOAMI on a structural error.
  - Fragile ~439KB contiguous kmalloc      -> bounded kvmalloc + DL_MAX_BLOB.
  - Stale ACK correlation                  -> per-op seq/rel_seq snapshots,
      cleared per op; unsigned-char wrap; explicit NACK; duplicate/arbitrary
      bcm_ssi_rx data ignored.
  - Text "Crc" ambiguity                   -> BlobLength validated vs decoded
      count; PatchAddress requires explicit hex.
  - 36B ttyBCM vs 32B direct-SSI autobaud  -> phase-1 uses direct-SSI 32 x
      0x80; vendor bcm477x_rpc_get_version has a broken inverted poll loop and
      must not be a sync authority.

Compile-verified: ssp_bbd.o, bbd.o, bcm_gps_spi.o, bcm_gps_mem.o,
bcm_gps_regs.o, ssp_sysfs.o, ssp_dev.o, ssp_i2c.o, gyro_lsm6dsl.o build with
aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu-gcc 15.2 (no new warnings).

Still required before flash (Stage 03/04): vendor frame/CRC/seq/ACK parity;
rpc_id transport-vs-operational semantics; KASAN/lockdep build.

Signed-off-by: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
